;; A MINT that puts one field in TWO oneofs.
;;
;; A proto field belongs to at most one oneof, so this declaration has no
;; truthful emission — and the failure is SILENT rather than loud, which is why
;; it is refused instead of left to protoc. `projection/oneof-of` takes the
;; FIRST oneof carrying a number, so with the refusal removed `raw` joins
;; `primary`, `secondary` emits with `scaled` alone, and the resulting file
;; compiles cleanly while saying something the mint did not.
;;
;; Both fields are real and pinned: the ONLY fault here is the double
;; membership, so a refusal on this input cannot be attributed to anything else.
{"pgbad.Reading"
 {:kind :message
  :name "Reading"
  :fields [{:name "raw" :type :uint32}
           {:name "scaled" :type :double}]
  :oneofs [{:name "primary" :required false :fields ["raw"]}
           {:name "secondary" :required false :fields ["raw" "scaled"]}]}}
